WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.022
Your body can stay healthy,
and a lot of that is up to you.

2
00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:12.701
Medicines. Vaccines. Moving every
day. And how to prove a point.

3
00:00:13.201 --> 00:00:16.451
A medicine is a substance
that treats an illness.

4
00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:20.247
The right amount helps you.
The wrong amount can harm you.

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.300
So a grown-up measures
the dose on the label.

6
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.375
More is not better. Double
the dose can poison you.

7
00:00:27.595 --> 00:00:31.728
Medicines are kept locked away.
Nobody ever takes someone else's.

8
00:00:32.228 --> 00:00:35.711
Some illnesses spread from
one living thing to another.

9
00:00:35.931 --> 00:00:40.110
Germs carry them. A cold.
Measles. A blight on potatoes.

10
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.463
Illnesses that spread like that
are called infectious diseases.

11
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:48.213
Plants and animals catch
them too, not only people.

12
00:00:48.713 --> 00:00:53.636
The first time a new germ gets in, your
body must work out how to fight it.

13
00:00:53.856 --> 00:00:57.803
That takes days. While your
body learns, you are ill.

14
00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:02.667
A vaccine is a harmless piece of
a germ, given while you are well.

15
00:01:02.887 --> 00:01:06.277
Your body learns to fight
it, and you do not get ill.

16
00:01:06.497 --> 00:01:11.559
Then if the real germ gets in, your
body is ready. It fights it fast.

17
00:01:11.779 --> 00:01:15.308
Puppies, kittens and farm
animals are vaccinated too.

18
00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:20.359
Your body is built to move. Sit
still all day and it gets weaker.

19
00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:25.409
Muscles that work get stronger.
Muscles that never work get smaller.

20
00:01:25.629 --> 00:01:30.505
The heart is a muscle too. Running
makes it beat faster and get stronger.

21
00:01:30.725 --> 00:01:34.441
Bones stay strong. You sleep
better and you feel better.

22
00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:39.119
It is not only sport. Walking,
dancing and playing all count.

23
00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:43.055
When you make a point about
health, back it up with evidence.

24
00:01:43.275 --> 00:01:46.758
Evidence is something that was
measured, counted or tested.

25
00:01:46.978 --> 00:01:51.204
I think PE is boring is an
opinion. Nobody measured it.

26
00:01:51.424 --> 00:01:56.858
Doctors measured stronger hearts in
children who ran. That is evidence.

27
00:01:57.358 --> 00:02:01.166
Science is not only in a lab.
It is used in your own area.

28
00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:05.566
A pharmacist knows each medicine,
and how much of it is safe.

29
00:02:05.786 --> 00:02:11.080
A nurse gives vaccines. A vet
vaccinates puppies and farm animals.

30
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.433
A PE teacher plans movement that
keeps a whole school healthy.

31
00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:20.112
The right medicine, the right
amount, a grown-up in charge.

32
00:02:20.332 --> 00:02:25.162
Infectious diseases spread. A
vaccine gets your body ready first.

33
00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:29.190
Move every day: muscles,
heart, bones, sleep and mood.

34
00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:34.333
Back your point with evidence, and ask
the people who use science near you.
